Reference lines of floating-vector-lanes.c (L05), recorded 2026-10-21.

Each line is one operation of one build: the form, the vector kind, the
rounding mode, the operation name and the 64-bit hash that main prints.
"plain" builds use -std=gnu11 -ffp-contract=off and hash the result bits.
"strict" builds add -frounding-math -DFLAGS -DMODE=m and also hash the
sticky flags that each vector operation raises, in rounding mode m. The
"sample-" forms add -DSAMPLE, which keeps every pair of operand values.

The same 600 lines came from every reference build, at -O0 and at -O2:
GCC 14.2.0 (Debian 14.2.0-19) and Clang 19.1.7 (Debian 19.1.7-3+b1) in
evo-nexlab:sealed (image e8d52bdced1f, linux/arm64, no network, glibc 2.41,
linked with -lm), and Apple clang 21.0.0 (clang-2100.1.1.101) on
arm64-apple-darwin25.6.0. The nan2 lines hash a count of zero: no reference
commutes the two-NaN lanes of + or * in these shapes.

